Level 1

2 rooms, very introductory. Simple accessible button to open the exit. Lots of spaces to create portals, but you can just do it by jumping. Really just a space to learn the keys

Level 2
2 rooms, learning how to move vertically with portals. Introduces pads, spawners and cubes. Sounds good, but needs rebuilding. Too fiddly!

Level 3
2 rooms, introducing lasers and barriers. Has the first real puzzle, which I like, but needs more space to breathe. Introduction to fizzlers, and the player needs to learn how to think laterally to overcome obstacles. Players are expected to try different strategies. Play tested well, but need polish

Level 4
2 rooms, possibly swap with level 3. First map is good, second is too fiddly. No real theme, and only a little charm

Level 5
2 rooms, and the whole thing is just coming up with the strategy of flinging. Once two-room shaft to fall down and get across. Very simple once you understand flinging, but I think badly undercooked.

Level 6
6 rooms, and the first level with a proper sense of space. No deep theme, but plenty of jumping around and portalling. Introduces two new strategies: 1. leave a portal outside a danger area as an exit route, 2. Jumping up into a new map, firing a portal and falling back down. Basically fine.

Level 7
First of the real challenging levels. The base concepts are coming up with bouncy elevators to reach inaccessible parts of the rooms; and leaving one anchoring portal and moving the second portal where you need it in stages. Good level.

Level 8
Mixed bag level, introduces sentries. Good start with a nice vertical climb, and a little trap to get Chell with a sentry on the first play through. Purpose of the level is really introducing sentries as enemies, but also potentially shows that sentries can be carried like cubes. Has a cube but for no purpose. Badly undercooked.

Level 9
Large 6 room level, lots of nice little bit but the theme got a little lost. This was the first 'labyrinth' level, twisty passages to the side; collect items from one area to use in anouther. Has a nasty trap at one end. Undercooked and fiddly. Has the first instance of needing to stand on a cube to access an area

Level 10
First 9 room level, with some good concepts. Themeatically good exploration of sentries. We have use a cube to block a sentry fire, we have to carry a sentry and use it on a pad instead of cube, and we have close a barrier to block the sentry. Nice.

Level 11
Great, but difficult four map level of one long vertical climb. Involves using bouncy elevators to move up in stages to get a cube to take all the way back to the bottom. Needs planning and skill, and satisfying to beat. Strong concept well delivered

Level 12
4 rooms, but feels larger. Introduces zappers, which surely need to get into some of these undercooked earlier levels. Introduces inverted barriers that close when others open, Very strong concepts of having to go through multiple stages to open and close obstacles, carefully plan portals to progress. Introduces blocking barriers with cubes. Strong level

Level 13
Another labyrinth level that feels cramped because of it. Full 9 rooms, but in three distinct areas. First area involves retreiving a sentry and bringing back to the centre. Then using complex elevator to get a laser, then finally dropping sentry into pad underneath acid to open exit. Very thematically strong of needing to continue to use the sentry in new areas once you think you've finished with it, and provides technical challenges in getting the sentry into each area. Difficult, and satisfying, but some parts are cramped. Strong level



